    @song_id, 'c4561e735c4e7301', '{"sectionCatalogRows":[199],"sectionCatalogMatchStatus":"matched"}', NULL, 'Rock Classics of the 70''s', '1973-11-02', '1973-11-02', 'https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Music/92/5e/d3/mzi.okyumwks.jpg/100x100bb.jpg', 'eng', '["eng"]', '["Pop"]', 'It''s nine o''clock on a Saturday
The regular crowd shuffles in
There''s an old man sittin'' next to me
Makin'' love to his tonic and gin

He says, "Son can you play me a memory?
